# decision pyproject.toml uses minimal line-oriented edits

The PyPI adapter edits only the matching `[project].dependencies` item and
`[tool.uv.sources]` key. A general TOML marshal is not used because the available small Go TOML
libraries do not preserve comments and formatting. The editor refuses an unsupported table
shape instead of rewriting the document. Fixtures cover multiline PEP 621 arrays, existing and
new uv source tables, idempotent wiring, and unwiring. Drift inspection is scoped to the
requested export's dependency/source entry and compares both the normalised git URL and the
locked commit; it must not accidentally match another git dependency elsewhere in the file.
